                    {
                        "form_id": "974fd3c5-49a0-4fc5-948e-b56458ef28cc",
                        "entry_id": "ced6ed09-1c4f-388d-914b-d81663acf8e4",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural",
                            "prepositional"
                        ],
                        "form": "луна́тиках"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "ec4ed2a8-247c-30c8-9b93-24740c7271f3",
                        "entry_id": "ced6ed09-1c4f-388d-914b-d81663acf8e4",
                        "glosses": [
                            "разг. тот, кто страдает лунатизмом (сомнамбулизмом, хождением во сне); сомнамбула"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "5a6d9344-1b93-4dff-9068-32178c0de60d",
                                "sense_id": "ec4ed2a8-247c-30c8-9b93-24740c7271f3",
                                "text": "Известно, например, что лунатики совершают самые опасные воздушные путешествия с такою ловкостью, на какую неспособен человек в полном сознании."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "87798392-f0aa-37ce-99d2-ac55bb2933e4",
                        "entry_id": "ced6ed09-1c4f-388d-914b-d81663acf8e4",
                        "glosses": [
                            "перен., разг. невменяемый, неадекватно поступающий человек"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "99f62c27-ee84-4a44-b085-3c409ba0913e",
                                "sense_id": "87798392-f0aa-37ce-99d2-ac55bb2933e4",
                                "text": "Как лунатик, шатаясь, шепча, поднялась Анисья с лавки, вытянула из окошка полушубок, свернула, кинула на лавку, в изголовье…"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "ae0a516c-35bf-436c-828f-e733409f80d2",
                                "sense_id": "87798392-f0aa-37ce-99d2-ac55bb2933e4",
                                "text": "Затем прошёл месяц, в течение которого два человека пересекали Аларгетскую равнину с достоинством и упорством лунатиков, странствующих по жёлобу крыши, смотря на луну."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "0ffe9e05-c662-4042-bac9-a51a6404d563",
                                "sense_id": "87798392-f0aa-37ce-99d2-ac55bb2933e4",
                                "text": "А ведь таких людей большинство, и именно эти лунатики определяют судьбу нашего мира."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "8a8a91ed-d76b-45c6-9b05-ab3a7321522f",
                        "source_entry_id": "ced6ed09-1c4f-388d-914b-d81663acf8e4",
                        "source_sense_description": "тот, кто страдает лунатизмом",
                        "target_lang_word": "sleepwalker",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "sleepwalker",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "a95d4d16-c057-3c12-ae23-5219f11670dc",
                                        "entry_id": "95772d19-8e92-33ef-8bde-1ea489628541",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A somnambulist; one who walks, or is active, while asleep."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "0ba48ce5-9630-4dec-b4a8-b62483b2a03f",
                                                "sense_id": "a95d4d16-c057-3c12-ae23-5219f11670dc",
                                                "text": "Edward Churchill still attended to his work in a hopeless mechanical manner like a sleep-walker who walks safely on a well-known round. But his Roman collar galled him, his cossack stifled him, his biretta was as uncomfortable as a merry-andrew's cap and bells."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c44e3816-06ea-4dcd-8290-1c64cb81162c",
                                                "sense_id": "a95d4d16-c057-3c12-ae23-5219f11670dc",
                                                "text": "Ashley looked dull as a sleepwalker and, as he came to her and put his hand upon her arm, he spoke like a sleepwalker."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "91892725-0f60-40ad-a526-f0333f94ba53",
                                                "sense_id": "a95d4d16-c057-3c12-ae23-5219f11670dc",
                                                "text": "Second, in the \"hypnotized\" subject, but not in the sleepwalker, characteristics such as a blank stare, a rigid facial expression, and an unwillingnes to talk have been produced by suggestions to become relaxed, drowsy, and sleepy and they can be easily removed by suggestions — for example, by suggestions to be alert."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "251dd72e-ecee-48e2-97eb-6c26f1a68572",
                                                "sense_id": "a95d4d16-c057-3c12-ae23-5219f11670dc",
                                                "text": "I was a sleepwalker, incapable of controlling or recalling my nocturnal activities."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "0999b6dc-9370-4283-b0bb-9f2b7bde94d1",
                                                "sense_id": "a95d4d16-c057-3c12-ae23-5219f11670dc",
                                                "text": "Consider, for example, the sleepwalker who goes into her neighbor's yard, takes an apple from the tree, and eats it ."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "416312c2-c08f-3d51-bed8-9b6ed57da8ef",
                                        "entry_id": "95772d19-8e92-33ef-8bde-1ea489628541",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "One in a state of magnetic or mesmeric sleep; someone in a hypnotic trance."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "archaic"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ee506627-cea6-4ee4-91ef-57d7fabb9c9b",
                                                "sense_id": "416312c2-c08f-3d51-bed8-9b6ed57da8ef",
                                                "text": "Though the sleepwalker sat with closely bandaged and wadded eyes, and his back to the grimacing part of the company, he described everything they were doing with the most comic humour, and he asked, 'What in the world is that gentleman in the chair making such faces for, and what is he giving himself such trouble about? […]\""
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ba15acad-db29-4131-aeb5-2516f8cd9433",
                                                "sense_id": "416312c2-c08f-3d51-bed8-9b6ed57da8ef",
                                                "text": "But the sleepwalker does much that is correct . The magnetic somnambulists are not dreaming ~ such that there is an accidental connection of images;~rather they know of themselves what they are, but as feeling beings they know this through their genius."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "3e8a70be-825a-430a-ac2b-23774cdcda34",
                                                "sense_id": "416312c2-c08f-3d51-bed8-9b6ed57da8ef",
                                                "text": "CALIGARI (Relaxing a bit.) I would like to apply for a permit to present my exhibit at your fair.\nCLERK. Oh. Then you're here to make money rather than to spend it. (Sighs) What kind of exhibit?\nCALIGARI. A somnambulist.\nCLERK. A somn-what?\nCALIGARI. A somnambulist, a sleepwalker."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "84ff39bd-77ed-33a4-b2ca-f052419e4403",
                                        "entry_id": "95772d19-8e92-33ef-8bde-1ea489628541",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A person from whom a voodoo practitioner (a bocor) has taken over control of their mind, making them a zombie who must do the bocor's bidding."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "3bb11c88-0f08-435a-a4fe-54764f7285ec",
                                                "sense_id": "84ff39bd-77ed-33a4-b2ca-f052419e4403",
                                                "text": "But don't zombies exist in real life— such as the Haitian zombies called “sleepwalkers\" ?"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ee348990-cebe-4415-9146-c57a39b94452",
                                                "sense_id": "84ff39bd-77ed-33a4-b2ca-f052419e4403",
                                                "text": "These were not the rotting corpses of the modern zombie apocalypse; rather they were laborers and sleepwalkers that served their masters dutifully."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "7e0e06a7-cf2a-4a84-ac77-546b9c6572af",
                                                "sense_id": "84ff39bd-77ed-33a4-b2ca-f052419e4403",
                                                "text": "However, I suffer the loss of slumber with waking dreams of what I am to become, a sleepwalker, living a nightmare, and that's the way it goes ."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "be58134b-2d74-3e17-a8b3-09124233f447",
                                        "entry_id": "95772d19-8e92-33ef-8bde-1ea489628541",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "One who goes though life in a state of obliviousness."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "figuratively"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "7c94eabd-7488-4eb2-b566-9fea7c824db1",
                                                "sense_id": "be58134b-2d74-3e17-a8b3-09124233f447",
                                                "text": "Perhaps he should have killed the white man, who, after all, is the dangerous one, the sleepwalker, the blind man . Getting rid of him would have protected \" the higher interests of society \" on three counts : It would have made this dreamer and sleepwalker \"pay the price\" for refusing to awaken to the truth of human identity; it would have destroyed the dreamer's \"dream world,\" which excludes blacks; and it would have carried out the narrator's \" responsibility,\" as \"invisible victim,\" for \" the fate of all\"—for those both within and without the sleepwalker's dream world."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e981f779-1fcf-4574-90db-d8204b135fc0",
                                                "sense_id": "be58134b-2d74-3e17-a8b3-09124233f447",
                                                "text": "These lines, stylistically reminiscent of Dante's guided tour of damned souls in the Inferno and written in a similar terza rima meterical pattern, survey the human condition, seeing hellish lineaments written on the faces of human souls—not because of any particular sin but as the after-effect of a staining caused by submitting to the triumph of life, suggesting the notion of existence as a process of unabating lapse and disfiguration, a hopeless enterprise where human action, bereft of beauteous shape, has not meaning, and all are, or soon will be, sleepwalkers oblivious to poetic truth."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6cbd6f0c-57c8-4f9e-8eed-b2c606cc407a",
                                                "sense_id": "be58134b-2d74-3e17-a8b3-09124233f447",
                                                "text": "Thus the Republicans, meeting in Philadephia in June to pick their candidate for president, passed over such party favorites—all conservative isolationists—as senators Robert A. Taft of Ohio and Arthur H. Vandenberg of Michigan and Governor Thomas E. Dewey of New York, men whom Walter Lippmann had called \"sleepwalkers” oblivious of the nation's crisis."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "a6e77fe1-eb42-4b6c-a044-1650ef6eb4c9",
                        "source_entry_id": "ced6ed09-1c4f-388d-914b-d81663acf8e4",
                        "source_sense_description": "тот, кто страдает лунатизмом",
                        "target_lang_word": "somnambulist",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "somnambulist",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "b5ae3289-c366-365b-b2f7-6ae0628c8c88",
                                        "entry_id": "8b7ca863-5e63-390d-b627-75dc9c5f966d",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A person who walks about in their sleep; a sleepwalker."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "07f75cf9-b1be-4478-839f-ae1e742a617c",
                                                "sense_id": "b5ae3289-c366-365b-b2f7-6ae0628c8c88",
                                                "text": "The clergyman floundered a moment, as is usual with an absent man who is recovering the train of his ideas, or a somnambulist when he is suddenly awakened."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "916d33eb-0708-4653-a904-17c2b58bce60",
                                                "sense_id": "b5ae3289-c366-365b-b2f7-6ae0628c8c88",
                                                "text": "The slim one got up and walked straight at me - still knitting with downcast eyes - and only just as I began to think of getting out of her way, as you would for a somnambulist, stood still, and looked up."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "74659091-27bf-4455-8eca-40cc38651c31",
                                                "sense_id": "b5ae3289-c366-365b-b2f7-6ae0628c8c88",
                                                "text": "He must have promptly rejected an alternative explanation which would better fulfill the demands of verisimilitude (“My wife, poor thing, in her nervous condition, now is afflicted also with sleepwalking!”), seeing the laborious tasks to which the resumed somnambulist devotes herself: kneeling at the edge of a pit, she anoints the earth with murky philters (unless the implements she holds in her hand are to be interpreted actually as acetylene torches scattering sparks, to melt the lead seals of a coffin)."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "e45c32fc-e892-4529-a2a4-b26dea19fea2",
                        "source_entry_id": "ced6ed09-1c4f-388d-914b-d81663acf8e4",
                        "source_sense_description": "невменяемый, неадекватно поступающий человек",
                        "target_lang_word": "lunatic",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "lunatic",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "66cc7b45-0a65-3a56-a19a-1e193df4699c",
                                        "entry_id": "29f24dfb-f140-381c-aa6a-1256444accb6",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "An insane person."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a7e21d48-4081-43e4-80b0-2da56e7f1854",
                                                "sense_id": "66cc7b45-0a65-3a56-a19a-1e193df4699c",
                                                "text": "While there are other races (or individuals—heaven forgive me, I am no ethnologist) who think you a criminal or a lunatic unless you carefully plod along from step to step like a hippopotamus out of water."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c0fdf044-75e6-4630-ae89-61c6bbe7b650",
                                                "sense_id": "66cc7b45-0a65-3a56-a19a-1e193df4699c",
                                                "text": "You may be right\nI may be crazy\nOh, but it just may be a lunatic you're looking for"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "lunatic",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "919627e7-ffdf-3c9b-9feb-09f4e64839a4",
                                        "entry_id": "d228d122-5c94-3581-8421-54907168dfef",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Crazed, mad, insane, demented."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "16374634-d0a4-366a-b264-8fa869df9a61",
                                        "entry_id": "d228d122-5c94-3581-8421-54907168dfef",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Relating to the Moon; lunar."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "literary",
                                            "rare"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "2370c0cf-bde5-4ceb-bdfa-47f5e8c518cd",
                                                "sense_id": "16374634-d0a4-366a-b264-8fa869df9a61",
                                                "text": "As the narrator turns his attention to the moon itself and its Lunatic inhabitants, Heinsius seems to draw on the True History, but is still within the confines of the Icaromenippus."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "70da88a6-946f-4697-8477-726284e1d8be",
                                                "sense_id": "16374634-d0a4-366a-b264-8fa869df9a61",
                                                "text": "That or I might bounce off something I hit and head back out into space, become the light in the eye of some lunatic observer, looking up at the big blue ball and seeing me bang something in their retina."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "b3992182-e050-3ccb-acfc-94a759da2e04",
                                        "entry_id": "d228d122-5c94-3581-8421-54907168dfef",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Influenced or affected by the Moon."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "literary",
                                            "rare"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "fd31f492-2b86-4c36-a76a-c0e1d49c3151",
                                                "sense_id": "b3992182-e050-3ccb-acfc-94a759da2e04",
                                                "text": "This I remember: she was false as the lunatic sea."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
